; EVERY FIGURE ABOVE IS INDICATIVE, AND THAT IS PART OF THE RULE RATHER THAN A FOOTNOTE.
; brain:booking_flow:92 says the prices are indicative and may differ, and that the exact one is
; named by a manager. That lands exactly on DECISIONS.md D11: the door is the price authority, a
; file never is, and when the door is silent the answer is that a human quotes this price -- not an
; average, not a range offered as a quote, not a number at all.
; WHAT THIS FILE DECLARES IS WHAT THE SHOP PUBLISHES. Publishing a tariff is not quoting a fee.
; A consumer may show the ladder as the shop's published tariff; it may not put any figure here in
; front of a client as that client's delivery price. This file computes no client-facing number, and
; the distinction is declared rather than trusted to a reader's good sense.
