pub const OFF_LADDER_NOTE : str = "A district the ladder does not name yields FEE_ABSENT, which turbobaby/pricing-honesty renders as a dash carrying the sentence that a human quotes the price. No neighbouring district's fee, no step boundary and no distance produces a number for it, and there is no function in this file that could. This is now a NARROW refusal where it used to be the whole section: twelve districts and one airport-adjacent case are published, and what remains unpublished is named. brain:business_rules:1426-1429 names five sheet zones (Phuket Town, Cape Panwa, Thalang East, Thalang North, Naithon) and a 1490 belt step as existing but explicitly unconfirmed by the owner, so they are the shape of the gap rather than candidates to fill it. CORRECTED 2026-09-24: the owner filled the gap directly that day for the shipped zone table -- the five at the sheet's prices and the airport at 690 -- so a district off the LADDER may now have a fee from the ZONE TABLE (zone_fee_thb). What survives is the interpolation ban: a district in neither table has no fee, and none is derived from a neighbour, a step or a distance.";
; Off the island the brain says exactly what the seed says and nothing more: delivery is Phuket only
; (brain:business_rules:10, brain:knowledge_base:404, brain:faq:96), an address off the island means
; no delivery and the client collects the bike. There is no off-island fee, no surcharge, no longer
; window and no exception, and the brain publishes none -- so none is declared, and the refusal below
; stays a refusal AFTER the read rather than for want of one.
pub const OFF_ISLAND_RULE_IS_ONLY_NO_DELIVERY : bool = true;
pub const OFF_ISLAND_FEE_SOURCES_FOUND : i32 = 0;
pub const OFF_ISLAND_NOTE : str = "Three brain nodes and the seed agree and none goes further than the boundary: delivery is Phuket only and an address or Maps link off the island means no delivery, with the client collecting the bike. Nothing anywhere publishes an off-island fee, a surcharge, a partial-way handover or a longer window, so this file declares none. The one neighbouring rule that sounds like an exception is a different fact and is already separated above: brain:faq:111 permits RIDING a rented bike to other islands and provinces, with recovery to Phuket at the client's cost if it breaks down. That is where a rented bike may go, not where the shop will bring one.";

; --- THE SHIPPED ZONE TABLE: the owner's Phuket zones -------------------------------------------
; REWRITTEN 2026-09-24, by the owner's decisions in chat that day. Until then this section was
; titled "The shipped zone table, which describes another island": src/delivery.rs shipped five
; default zones -- four Koh Phangan villages and one handover row -- the database held the same
; four villages from migrations/071_delivery_zones_koh_phangan.sql, and none of the four lay on the
; coverage island. Those facts are kept below under _BEFORE_PHUKET names: they were true until
; this change and an old order still references those rows.
; THE DECISIONS, four of them. (1) The table is the owner's live delivery sheet -- all sixteen of
; its zones at the sheet's own prices -- plus the two districts the brain's delivery rule names and
; the sheet lacks, Kathu at 490 and Naiharn at 590 (brain:business_rules:625-630, the same lines on
; the 2026-09-21 and 2026-09-24 reads). Paklok's 490 and Maikhao's 990 are the owner's decisions of
; 2026-09-06, declared above, and the airport's 690 is the owner's choice on 2026-09-24 from the rule's
; 590-690 range. Eighteen zones. (2) No delivery time in minutes: none is published. (3) The Koh
; Phangan rows are deactivated, not deleted; the shop's own pickup row stays active at fee 0.
; (4) The sheet's out-of-belt settings and the 17:30 cut-off are not modelled by this change; the
; section after the ETA note names both.
; THE SHEET IS NOT A FILE IN THIS REPOSITORY. It is the owner's Bridge sheet, read here through the
; PC bot's read-only snapshot fixtures/delivery_zones_get.live.json in the turbobaby-bot repository,
; taken 2026-07-15, rows [name, lat, lon, price, radius]. Like a brain line, that path resolves
; nowhere in this tree and no gate checks it. The anchors' coordinates and radii were not imported:
; delivery_zones has no coordinate column and this change adds none.
; WHERE THE ROWS LIVE. migrations/087_delivery_zones_phuket.sql inserts the eighteen, idempotent by
; name_en, at sort orders 1-18; the pickup row keeps 0 and stays the picker's default.
; src/delivery.rs:57-76 carries the same eighteen in the same order, behind the pickup row
; (:45-50), as the built-in table. ORDER IS NOT RANK here either: it is the tariff's own order --
; ladder step, cheapest first; within a step the sheet's row order; Kathu and Naiharn close their
; step. The English names are the owner's spelling of 2026-09-24 (Bang Tao, Pa Khlok, Mai Khao, Nai
; Harn), not the one-word form the ladder spells after the seed's Bangtao (Bangtao, Paklok,
; Maikhao, Naiharn); PHUKET_ZONE_LADDER_INDEX joins the two tables without renaming either.
; EVERY FEE HERE IS INDICATIVE, exactly as the ladder's is: the zone table is what the shop
; publishes, and the price a client pays is named by a human (D11, EVERY_PUBLISHED_FEE_IS_INDICATIVE).
