pub const ZONE_ROWS_KEPT_REASON : str = "Three recorded reasons, none of them an oversight. migrations/060_delivery_zones.sql:16-19 seeded one mainland placeholder zone to match an older hard-coded fallback. migrations/071_delivery_zones_koh_phangan.sql:13-18 deactivates that placeholder rather than deleting it, because placed orders reference delivery_zone_id and deleting the row would orphan them, and :9-11 leaves 060 itself unedited because an applied migration may not be rewritten. migrations/085_unpublish_woody_catalog.sql:32-38 renames only the handover row and states that the island zone names are the other shop's delivery map, kept until the owner defines TurboBaby's Phuket zones -- flagged to him, not decided in code. DECISIONS.md D19 records the same thing as an unmade product call. A zone is a name, a fee and an ETA, and inventing any of the three would put an unmeasured number on a customer's screen (D11). CORRECTED 2026-09-24: the owner made that call. migrations/087_delivery_zones_phuket.sql deactivates the four Koh Phangan rows for the same reason 071 gave for the placeholder -- placed orders reference them -- and deletes nothing; the names and fees of the eighteen Phuket zones are the owner's, and the ETA is left absent, because none is published.";
; src/delivery.rs:103-116. One override, and a failure mode that used to point the wrong way:
