; --- What is not published, said plainly ----------------------------------------------------------
; The shop publishes a WINDOW, not a travel time. No ETA for any area appears in
; data/fleet_seed.json, and the minute ranges the API serves (src/api/orders.rs:1913-1914 and
; :2535-2536) come from the zone rows of the other island.
; CORRECTED 2026-09-24: the owner said so in as many words -- no delivery time in minutes is
; published, the shop promises windows. The API serves those two fields through one rule now,
; served_eta at src/delivery.rs:126-131 (reached through :133-141 from both lines above): both
; edges or neither, so a row without minutes is null and never a 0. No shipped row has minutes. The
; checkout prints an ETA line only for two present minutes and has no literal fallback left
; (src/ui/screens/checkout_screen.rs:822-825, :1546), the success screen likewise (:302-305,
; :490-495), and the admin write supplies no minutes of its own (src/api/admin.rs:1067-1072).
pub const ETA_IS_NOT_PUBLISHED : bool = true;
pub const OWNER_SAID_NO_ETA_IS_PUBLISHED_AT : str = "2026-09-24";
pub const API_SERVES_AN_ABSENT_ETA_AS_NULL : bool = true;
pub const A_HALF_STORED_ETA_IS_SERVED_AS_NULL : bool = true;
pub const ETA_RULE_SITE : str = "src/delivery.rs:126 served_eta";
pub const CHECKOUT_ETA_FALLBACK_LITERALS : i32 = 0;
pub const CHECKOUT_ETA_FALLBACK_LITERALS_BEFORE_2026_09_24 : i32 = 1;
pub const SUCCESS_SCREEN_ETA_FALLBACK_LITERALS : i32 = 0;
pub const SUCCESS_SCREEN_ETA_FALLBACK_LITERALS_BEFORE_2026_09_24 : i32 = 1;
pub const ADMIN_WRITE_SUPPLIES_NO_ETA : bool = true;
pub const ADMIN_WRITE_DEFAULTED_THE_ETA_BEFORE_2026_09_24 : bool = true;
pub const ETA_NOTE : str = "No travel-time estimate for any area of the coverage island exists in this repository. The shop's promise is a window with a start and a published length; the min/max minute pair the API returns is read from delivery_zones rows whose places are on another island, and the empty-list fallback on the checkout screen prints a single hard-coded '30-45' string that no source measures (src/ui/screens/checkout_screen.rs:829). What would be needed is an owner-measured time per Phuket area, which nobody has taken. Until then a window is the answer and an ETA is not offered. RE-MEASURED 2026-09-21 over all 43 tracked specs: still nothing. turbobaby/order-status, written that day, records No delivery ETA from its own side, which is a second contract arriving independently at the same absence and not a source that supplies one. The checkout-screen line was re-read the same day and still carries the hard-coded string. WIDENED 2026-09-21 past the repository: the owner's knowledge base was read on the same day the tariff ladder came out of it, and it publishes no travel time either. What it publishes about timing is a WINDOW and its floor -- the office opens at 10:00, the earliest window is 11:00-13:00, same-day delivery is two hours after the booking but never before that window, the default window is two hours and narrows to one on request (brain:knowledge_base:415-419, brain:faq:100-101) -- which is the same shape the seed already carries and is not an ETA. So this absence survived a search of the one place that answered the tariff question, and BRAIN_ETA_SOURCES_FOUND records that the search happened rather than leaving the claim resting on the repository alone. CORRECTED 2026-09-24: the owner settled it the same way -- no delivery time in minutes is published, the shop promises windows. Migration 087 stores no ETA on any zone row, the API serves null for both minute fields (served_eta, src/delivery.rs), and the literal '30-45' is gone from the checkout and from the success screen, which had a second copy this note never named. The absence is now the shipped state and not only a refusal.";
; Nothing in this repository decides whether an address is on the coverage island. delivery_zones
; carries name, name_en, fee, min_order, eta_min, eta_max, is_active and sort_order
; (migrations/060_delivery_zones.sql:2-14) and no geometry of any kind; the checkout screen can
; read browser coordinates but only pastes them into a free-text address field
; (src/ui/screens/checkout_screen.rs:210-245) and compares them with nothing. So the first
; argument of the readiness function is an input this repository cannot yet produce -- stated
; here rather than faked with a bounding box nobody measured.
pub const COVERAGE_BOUNDARY_IS_NOT_MACHINE_CHECKABLE : bool = true;
pub const COVERAGE_BOUNDARY_NOTE : str = "The coverage rule is a sentence, not a shape. No polygon, radius, centroid or geocoder is ever applied to a delivery address, and the delivery_zones table has no coordinate column, so on_coverage_island is answered by a human today. The tree is not free of coordinate machinery and the claim is deliberately narrower than that: quest_places and hunt_checkpoints carry lat/lon columns (migrations/003_quest.sql:6-7, migrations/021_hunt_checkpoints_fields.sql:5-6) and src/trios/quest.rs:86-90 measures a plain Euclidean distance between two of them. None of it is a geographic boundary, none of it reads a delivery address, and none of it touches delivery_zones. What is missing is a boundary with a source and a decision about what to do with an address that cannot be resolved. A default of true would deliver off the island; a default of false would refuse every legitimate order; neither is invented here.";
; The write end of the same defect as the render end. src/api/admin.rs:1038-1044 maps any
; non-finite or negative fee to 0.0 before storing it (:1084 on create, :1131-1133 on update), so
; an unmeasurable fee is persisted as free delivery rather than refused.
pub const ADMIN_WRITE_TURNS_AN_UNUSABLE_FEE_INTO_ZERO : bool = true;

; --- Two rules the shipped table knows about and does not model --------------------------------
; The owner's fourth decision of 2026-09-24: neither of these is modelled by the change that
; shipped the Phuket table, and both are named here so the absence is recorded, not discovered.
; (1) OUT-OF-BELT PRICING. The sheet's config rows carry OUT_BELT_KM 5, OUT_BELT_PRICE 1490 and
;     OUT_BEYOND "by agreement" (translated), in the snapshot named above. Three sources say three
;     different things and none is a rule this repository could apply: the PC bot's own resolver
;     (turbobaby-bot delivery.py, at its OUT_BELT constants, read 2026-09-24) keeps both numbers as
;     LEGACY and says it does not apply them; brain:business_rules:1426-1429 (:1417-1420 on the
;     2026-09-21 read) says the 1490 step is NOT confirmed by the owner; and the owner said on
;     2026-09-24 that it is not modelled now. So an address outside every zone has no fee here --
;     FEE_ABSENT, a human quotes it -- and 1490 is a step of no table in this file.
; (2) THE 17:30 CUT-OFF. DELIVERY_CUTOFF_MIN above is the owner's rule of 2026-08-20 and this file
;     models it as the third outcome it is. The shipped code does not: nothing under src/ compares
;     a delivery time with 17:30 (searched 2026-09-24), and the zone table has no time column.
pub const OUT_BELT_KM_IN_THE_SHEET : i32 = 5;
pub const OUT_BELT_PRICE_IN_THE_SHEET_THB : i32 = 1490;
pub const OUT_BEYOND_IN_THE_SHEET : str = "by agreement";
